<http://data.silknow.org/object/40cb8e67-3657-3df0-9d8c-55d57d1a83d0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s waistcoat with a round neckline, revers, straight fronts and straight hems reaching to the hip.  Each front has a welted pocket.  The fronts are made of white silk satin, the back of white woollen broadcloth.  The waistcoat and pockets are lined with bleached linen; the revers are faced with white silk satin, the front hems with white silk twill.  The waistcoat is embroidered-to-shape with black silk floss, silver and silver-gilt spangles and purl, white and pink pastes and tamboured with silver-gilt thread, in a pattern of abstract floral sprigs, swags and narrow border on the pocket welts and revers, below the pockets, around the front neck, edges and hems.  The waistcoat has a double-breasted effect with 10 worked buttonholes and 10 embroidered buttons on the left front and 10 embroidered buttons on the right front."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/40cb8e67-3657-3df0-9d8c-55d57d1a83d0> .

